---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { fitTitle, fitDesc, abs } from '../lib/seo';
import { RELEASE } from '../lib/pages';

const title = fitTitle(['Disclaimer: font licence summaries are not legal advice', 'Disclaimer: licence summaries are not legal advice']);
const description = fitDesc([
  'Fontwell’s licence verdicts are plain-English readings of public licence texts, not legal advice. What that means, its limits, and what to do for big uses.',
  'Fontwell’s licence verdicts are plain-English readings of public licence texts, not legal advice. What that means, where the limits are, and what to do for high-stakes uses.',
  'Fontwell’s licence verdicts are plain-English readings of public licence texts, not legal advice. What this means, where the limits are and what to do for high-stakes uses.',
]);
const crumbs = [{ name: 'Desk', path: '/' }, { name: 'Disclaimer', path: '/disclaimer/' }];
const ld = [{ '@type': 'WebPage', name: 'Disclaimer', url: abs('/disclaimer/'), dateModified: RELEASE }];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/disclaimer/" og="/og/about.png" ld={ld} crumbs={crumbs}>
  <article class="prose">
    <div class="kicker">Disclaimer</div>
    <h1>Is Fontwell’s licence information legal advice?</h1>
    <p class="lede" data-answer>No. Fontwell explains public font licences in plain English and names the clause behind each answer, but it does not know your project, your jurisdiction or facts outside the licence text. For high-stakes uses, read the font’s own licence and ask a qualified lawyer.</p>
    <h2>What our verdicts cover</h2>
    <p>Verdicts in the <a href="/tools/license-checker/">licence checker</a> and on family pages apply fixed rules written from the SIL Open Font License 1.1, the Apache License 2.0 and the Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0. They describe what those licences permit in general. They do not cover trademarks, contracts you have signed, platform rules, privacy law or the laws of a particular country.</p>
    <h2>Which licence applies</h2>
    <p>We identify a family’s licence from the folder it sits in on the google/fonts repository at the snapshot date. A font obtained elsewhere, or an older or newer version, may carry a different licence. The licence file distributed with your copy of the font is authoritative.</p>
    <h2>Data freshness</h2>
    <p>All figures show the date of the snapshot they come from. Google may add, rename or update families after that date. See the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a>.</p>
    <h2>Advertising and affiliate links</h2>
    <p>Fontwell is funded by advertising. Labelled affiliate links, where present, do not influence licence verdicts, which are generated by the same rules for every family.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
